(7196117, 1106510, 37252, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by blindjustice:</b></div><hr/><i> I love the mystery of this shot- are you stopped, because the bus has its lights and arm out, and are those grape vines, concord grapes, or some northern vineyard located on a wine tour of a state not typically known for wine? or are they vines at all? could be a new orchard. <br/> <br/>fun to ponder, whatever the rural truth is. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The arm of the bus is not out (have to zoom in to see that) and the lights were nto on, but the sun was reflecting off them. We were both moving at about 50mph. Yes, those are grape vines. The Old Mission Peninsula is one vineyard after another , mixed in with orchards. If spring ever comes about the flowering trees will be beautiful.</td>', 'Originally posted by blindjustice: I love the mystery of this shot- are you stopped, because the bus has its lights and arm out, and are those grape vines, concord grapes, or some northern vineyard located on a wine tour of a state not typically known for wine? or are they vines at all? could be a new orchard.  fun to ponder, whatever the rural truth is.   The arm of the bus is not out (have to zoom in to see that) and the lights were nto on, but the sun was reflecting off them. We were both moving at about 50mph. Yes, those are grape vines. The Old Mission Peninsula is one vineyard after another , mixed in with orchards. If spring ever comes about the flowering trees will be beautiful.', '2014-03-31 02:04:38.000000', NULL, 0),
